      "updated": 1772699351771,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Collision:\nNow, if we are applying linear chaining and division rule and we find that all elements of an array get stored \nin a single index, then we will call it a case of collision.\n\nExample:\n\nGiven array: [8, 18, 28, 38, 48, 58, 68, ….., 1008]",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Collision:\nNow, if we are applying linear chaining and division rule and we find that all elements of an array get stored \nin a single index, then we will call it a case of collision.\n\nExample:\n\nGiven array: [8, 18, 28, 38, 48, 58, 68, ….., 1008]",
